WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.712
Lab 1 needs only Python on a
laptop: no tenant, no network.

2
00:00:04.712 --> 00:00:06.851
You start with Microsoft's definition.

3
00:00:06.851 --> 00:00:11.421
The linter finds eight problems, and
when you run it for a GCC High tenant,

4
00:00:11.421 --> 00:00:16.612
the callback heads to the worldwide cloud
and the task fails at the end of the wait.

5
00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:19.644
Switch the cloud to
worldwide and it completes,

6
00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:22.675
which is exactly why the
problem is easy to miss.

7
00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:27.777
Then the program's definition: a clean
lint, and a GCC High run that survives

8
00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:33.020
two transient failures, does the work
once, and calls back to the right cloud.
